# [NULLABLE-ANCH] (lane nullanch1, 2026-10-08): THE FIVE MOVERS of the
# anchor-aware nullability decline (docs/dev/lanes/nullanch1_report.md;
# STEP 0 docs/dev/lanes/nullanch0_report.md). Each pattern is nullable, but
# every empty path crosses a non-multiline `^` AND `$`, so its empty match
# exists only on a subject that is empty up to a final newline. The
# `empty_admits` fact (src/facts/widths.c) is false for each, the prefilter
# decline lifts, and the artifact carries the exact hybrid prefilter
# (`RX_ENGINE_SEL "selected"`, `RX_VM_PREFILTER "hybrid"` — held by
# tests/codegen/run_prechecks.sh §11). The answers below do not depend on
# that: a prefilter is a filter.
#
# ORACLE FIRST. Every m/n/g line is libpcre2 10.46's answer, written by
# docs/dev/optloop/nullanch/pcre2_cells.py --rxt (transcript beside it,
# pcre2_transcript.txt), never pcrec's. Blocks without `# pcre2-only` are
# python-verified too. The `# pcre2-only` blocks are the subroutine-call
# patterns (python `re` has no call) and the two GIVE-UP CELLS: a near-miss
# long enough that the default VM, before this row, exhausted its step budget
# (PCREC_ERR_STEPS) where it now answers `nomatch` at once. libpcre2 itself
# hits its match limit there (-47, upstream_issues.md U4), so those two are
# verified by libpcre2 on the language-equal `^[a-z]*$` / `^\s*$` and by
# python `re` run once offline (7.9 s and 108 s, U19) — both in the
# transcript. With the decline back in place (sabotage S510) each give-up
# cell reds as a give-up.

# bench capability evil-alt-nested: short hits, a near-miss, the final-newline arm of `$`, and a start past 0
pattern ^(([a-z]+)*)+$
m "" 0 0
g 1 0 0
g 2 -1 -1
m "abc" 0 3
g 1 3 3
g 2 0 3
m "abc\n" 0 3
g 1 3 3
g 2 0 3
m "\n" 0 0
g 1 0 0
g 2 -1 -1
n "ab!"
n "a b"
n "aaaaaaaa!"
n "x\ny"
ns 1 "abc"

# THE GIVE-UP CELL: 17 letters and a non-letter. Before this row the default artifact had no prefilter and its VM gave up (PCREC_ERR_STEPS, ~2.2 s); the exact hybrid prefilter now dismisses it. python's backtracking `re` takes seconds here, hence pcre2-only
# pcre2-only
pattern ^(([a-z]+)*)+$
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!"

# bench capability trim-nested-star
pattern ^(\s+)*$
m "" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1
m "    " 0 4
g 1 0 4
n "  x"
m "\n" 0 1
g 1 0 1
m " \t \n" 0 4
g 1 0 4
n "x"
ns 2 "    "

# THE GIVE-UP CELL: 32 blanks and a non-blank (the default VM gave up before this row); pcre2-only for python's cost
# pcre2-only
pattern ^(\s+)*$
n "                                x"

# corpus d27_edge mover
pattern ^(a{2,4})?$
m "" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1
m "aa" 0 2
g 1 0 2
n "aaaaa"
m "\n" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1
m "aa\n" 0 2
g 1 0 2
n "aab"
ns 1 "aa"

# corpus sr_define/k69/quantified mover (a subroutine call: python has none)
# pcre2-only
pattern ^(a?)(?1)*$
features recursion
m "" 0 0
g 1 0 0
m "aaaa" 0 4
g 1 0 1
n "aaab"
m "\n" 0 0
g 1 0 0
m "aa\n" 0 2
g 1 0 1
n "b"
ns 1 "aa"

# corpus quantified mover (a subroutine call under a possessive star)
# pcre2-only
pattern ^(?:(?<g>a?)){0}(?&g)*+$
features recursion,named-groups,atomic-groups
m "" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1
m "aaa" 0 3
g 1 -1 -1
n "aab"
m "\n" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1
m "aa\n" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
ns 1 "aa"
